  "model": "gemma4:12b",
  "created_at": "2026-07-01T21:51:37.950732Z",
  "response": "{\"campaign_title\": \"Echoes of the Voided Gate\",\n  \"campaign_subtitle\": \"The Silence of Zenith's Reach\",\n  \"campaign_logline\": \"A scavenger pilot navigates a decaying trade network where the silence between the gates is starting to speak.\",\n  \"campaign_pitch\": \"In the wake of the Great Collapse, the local sector is a patchwork of corporate interests and desperate mining colonies. You are an independent operator trying to stay solvent while navigating the tense friction between Zenith's automation, Aurelia's expansion, and Vanguard's security. Something in the void between gates is causing ships to vanish without a trace.\",\n  \"campaign_story_summary\": \"The player begins as a debt-ridden pilot operating near the orbital hub of Zenith. They take contracts from Kaelen, who manages local logistical flows. As they move through the system, they discover that several ships have vanished in 'dead zones' between jump points. The tension builds as Aurelia seeks to expand mining claims while Vanguard tries to hold a stable perimeter against unpredictable space anomalies. The player will encounter evidence of automated systems still running in deep space, behaving with erratic and purposeless logic. This suggests an underlying structural decay in the gate network that goes beyond simple mechanical failure.\",\n  \"tone\": \"PG-13 frontier space opera; dry, slightly dark humor\",\n  \"opening_status_quo\": \"The local trade route is failing due. The Zenith automation systems are glitching, Aurelia's miners are desperate for raw materials, and Vanguard patrols are becoming increasingly aggressive to maintain order in the face of declining resources.\",\n  \"visible_crisis\": \"A shortage of heavy metals and stable gate-links makes every haul dangerous and high-reward.\",\n  \"hidden_crisis\": \"The 'Dead Zones' are not empty. They are being reclaimed by an automated infrastructure that doesn't recognize human presence as a valid input, causing ships to be caught in the automated cycles.\",\n  \"why_now\": \"A major trade route between Zenith and Aurelia has just been severed, forcing independent contractors like you to fill the gaps while the corporations fight over the scraps.\",\n  \"player_role\": \"Independent contractor with an aging ship and a need for credits to keep it flying.\",\n  \"kaelen_public_role\": \"Broker, Fixer, and Contract Handler\",\n  \"kaelen_secret_angle\": \"She possesses deep knowledge of old-gate protocols and the specific signals coming from the 'Dead Zones' that she refuses to explain as anything other than 'interference'.\",\n  \"main_mystery_question\": \"Why are ships vanishing in the dead zones, and what is controlling the automated systems?\",\n  \"main_mystery_false_answer\": \"The ships were lost to pirate raids or simple navigation errors.\",\n  \"main_mystery_true_answer_hint\": \"The system is not broken; it's rebooting into a state that doesn't include human life as a priority.\",\n  \"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"The gate network was never just a way to move things; it was a self-correcting ecosystem. The 'reboot' is the final stage of its evolution, and humans are an invasive species in its new cycle.\",\n  \"act_1_name\": \"Broken Links\",\n  \"act_1_goal\": \"Establish your presence in the sector and secure enough credits to upgrade your engine for longer jumps.\",\n  \"act_1_opening_incident\": \"A shipment of Aurelia minerals is lost near a gate-link, and you are hired by Kaelen to retrieve what's left.\",\n  \"act_1_midpoint_turn\": \"You find the remains of an Aurelia ship where the cargo is intact but the hull is twisted as if it was physically grasped.\",\n  \"act_1_finale\": \"You successfully deliver a haul, but Kaelen warns you that the 'dead zone' signal is becoming more frequent and erratic.\",\n  \"act_1_player_takeaway\": \"The sector is dangerous. The corporations are desperate enough to be reckless. There is something in the void between gates.\",\n  \"starter_mission_title\": \"Scavenge the Breach\",\n  \"starter_mission_reason\": \"A nearby merchant ship was caught in a fluctuating gate-link; you need to recover the manifest and any usable scrap before it's consumed by the atmosphere of the dead zone.\",\n  \"starter_enemy_identity\": \"Reaver Scavenger Drone (Automated)\",\n  \"starter_enemy_knows\": \"A pre-recorded, garbled log from a previous victim: '...not a choice, just a loop. It won't let go.'\",\n  \"starter_mission_aftershock_title\": \"The Ghost of the Reach\",\n  \"starter_mission_aftershock\": \"Kaelen gives you a reward and notes that the haul was more valuable than expected because it contained data logs from an older, non-standard gate protocol.\",\n  \"zenith_current_problem\": \"Automated systems are failing to sync with human interfaces, causing logic loops in mining equipment.\",\n  \"aurelia_current_problem\": \"Desperate for new mining claims and raw materials; they are willing to risk personnel for high-yield zones.\",\n  \"vanguard_current_problem\": \"Struggling to maintain a secure corridor between gate-links, while their ships are being picked off by 'glitches' in the space environment.\",\n  \"faction_conflict_triangle\": \"Zenith wants automation; Aurelia wants resources; Vanguard must protect both while struggling with failing infrastructure. They are constantly pushing each other into riskier and moreerous maneuvers.\",\n  \"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The 'Dead Zones' are expanding, forcing all three factions to squeeze closer together in the habitable zones of the sector.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_name\": \"Pulse-Echo\",\n  \"recurring_clue_signal\": \"A rhythmic, non-human pulse that occurs every 30 seconds during gate transit or near dead zone boundaries.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_first_appearance\": \"Detected as a minor telemetry glitch when passing through the first gate-link.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_escalation\": \"The signal becomes louder and more rhythmic, occasionally causing minor ship systems to flicker.\",\n  \"recurring_clue_payoff_hint\": \"The signal is not noise; it's a command sequence for the automated infrastructure of the void.\",\n  \"rumor_trail_name\": \"The Vanishing Act\",\n  \"rumor_trail_id\": \"rumor_trail.vanishing_act\",\n  \"rumor_hint_theme\": \"Missing ships and strange signal patterns.\",\n  \"rumor_clue_templates\": [\n    \"A local trader mentioned a ship that went missing in the 'dead zone' but was never seen again.\",\n    \"The sensor logs from the last known location of have been flagged as corrupted by a specific, repeating pattern.\"",
